  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Sustainable and responsible enterprises in Pakistan promoted</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">In 2026, ILO Pakistan will build on its experience in productivity upgrading, value chain development, green jobs and formalization to generate systemic impact on sustainable enterprises, competitiveness and productivity growth for decent work. The Office will institutionalize proven tools within national and provincial systems to ensure scale, sustainability and strong tripartite ownership.

ILO Pakistan will strengthen responsible business conduct by embedding the principles of the Tripartite Declaration and due diligence frameworks into national policies and sectoral strategies, particularly in export-oriented and climate-vulnerable sectors. It will support government institutions to operationalize human rights and environmental due diligence, while enabling employers&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; and workers&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; organizations to engage in meaningful social dialogue on wages, occupational safety and health, climate risks and supply chain transparency. By linking responsible business conduct to trade and competitiveness strategies, the Office will position decent work as a driver of resilience and market access.

ILO Pakistan will enhance access to business development and financial services by partnering with financial institutions, SME authorities and chambers of commerce. It will connect productivity upgrading and formalization with improved access to credit, green finance and digital advisory services. By scaling up approaches such as SCORE and WISE and promoting productivity-linked financing, the Office will strengthen enterprise sustainability and labour standards compliance.

ILO Pakistan will facilitate transition to the formal economy through coherent strategies aligned with Recommendation 204, promoting simplified registration, modernized labour inspection, social protection extension and incentive-based compliance.</narrative>
  </description>
